<!-- SpotBugs project decisions: a rule, or a rule in part of the code, that the team has decided not
     to enforce. One Match per decision, with a comment giving the reason, for example:

       <!- - JPA entities share associations by design (reason ...) - ->
       <Match><Package name="~team\.projectpulse\..*"/><Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP"/></Match>

     Unlike the baseline, this file may grow, but every entry is a reviewed decision. -->
<FindBugsFilter>
  <!-- D1: EI_EXPOSE_REP and EI_EXPOSE_REP2 off project-wide. Of the 219 findings baselined on
       2026-11-01: 144 are in JPA entities, whose associations must stay the live references
       Hibernate tracks (a defensive copy breaks dirty checking and lazy loading); 29 are Spring
       beans storing injected singletons through constructor injection; 34 are DTO records that are
       serialized to JSON and dropped; the other 12 are report/principal holders built and read once
       per request. None stores caller data across a trust boundary. -->
  <Match><Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP,EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/></Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
